---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Terms | HookEcho"
  description="Terms for the HookEcho website and its owner-operated YouTube publishing tool."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="lede">Effective September 5, 2026</p>

      <h2>HookEcho and StormDesk</h2>
      <p>
        HookEcho and StormDesk are open-source weather tools provided without warranties. They
        are not official warning sources or substitutes for instructions from public safety
        authorities. The software licenses in their repositories govern copying and distribution.
      </p>

      <h2>YouTube publishing tool</h2>
      <p>
        The HookEcho Promotion API client is private, owner-operated automation. It uploads our
        product media and metadata to the authorized HookEcho and StormDesk channels and reads
        aggregate channel analytics for project reporting. It is not offered to site visitors or
        third-party channel owners.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use of the client and YouTube features is also governed by the
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a>. Uploaded content
        must comply with those terms, the YouTube Community Guidelines, copyright law and privacy
        rights. Google may suspend or terminate API access for non-compliance.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy and access</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains the data the client accesses, stores
        and reports, along with revocation and deletion instructions. Questions can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:hookecho.io@gmail.com">hookecho.io@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  :global(section:first-of-type) {
    background-image: var(--mesh);
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-size: 100% 22rem;
  }
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-dim); }
</style>
